The way freeze should be used for debugging:

Freeze hangs machine, with current micro state
repeatedly executed.  While freezing, external LD STATE causes the
pads to turn around, reading external state number
onto bus, and "dispatching" to that location.  There
should be some dedicated defpc's that allow
the external kludge to look at all of the registers
(this may often be existing defpc's).
An external RD STATE gets the current state onto
the bus and out on the pads.
Both RD STATE and LD STATE will have to disable
the PH1*FROM-xx and probably PH1*TO-xx.
It may also be a good idea to allow
RD STATE to get at the GC-NEEDED bit, NANO-RUN,
NANO-STATE, etc.

